LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T152415Z
SEQUENCE:1786289055
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:Full-Body Athletic Strength
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3500 kcal\, 180 g protein\, 505 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: hit the higher protein target with 40-45 g protei
 n in 4 meals\, plus 50-80 g carbs before heavy lifting and carbs again af
 ter.\nCategory: gym\nRun volume: 0 km\n\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 7 min easy cardio\
 , squat-to-stand\, band pull-aparts\, push-ups\, and hinge ramp sets.\n\n
 \nMain Work:\n- Progression: double progression\; add load only when pres
 ses\, hinges\, and pulls are all stable at RPE 8 or lower.\n- Incline pre
 ss\, shoulder press\, or bench press: top set 1 x 6-8 at RPE 8\, then 2-3
  back-off sets x 8-10 at RPE 7-8.\n- Trap-bar deadlift or Romanian deadli
 ft: 2-3 x 5-6 at RPE 7-8\, leave 2-3 RIR.\n- Pull-ups or chest-supported 
 rows: 4 x 6-10 at RPE 8 paired with front-foot elevated split squat or ha
 ck squat 3 x 8-10 per leg at RPE 8.\n- Shoulder\, trap\, and quad finishe
 r: lateral raises 2-3 x 15-20\, dumbbell trap raise 2 x 12-15\, leg exten
 sion 2 x 12-15\, then weighted sit-ups 2 x 8-12.\n- Activation: light goo
 d mornings: 2 x 12-15 at RPE 5-6 using no more than 50% of normal working
  load\; stop if symptoms rise or the next morning is worse.\n\n\nFueling:
 \n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates
  before and after training.\n\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06
 :00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hubert-training-20260811@training-calendar
