SUMMARY:Lower Hypertrophy + Posterior Chain
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3500 kcal\, 180 g protein\, 505 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: hit the higher protein target with 40-45 g protei
 n in 4 meals\, plus 50-80 g carbs before heavy lifting and carbs again af
 ter.\nCategory: gym\nRun volume: 0 km\n\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 7-8 min bike\, spl
 it squat isometric holds\, ankle rocks\, and hinge ramp sets.\n\n\nMain W
 ork:\n- Progression: double progression\; add load only when tempo and kn
 ee control stay stable at RPE 8 or lower.\n- Bulgarian split squat or fro
 nt-foot elevated split squat: 4 x 8-10 per leg at RPE 7-8.\n- Romanian de
 adlift: 3 x 8 at RPE 7-8 paired with leg press or hack squat 3 x 10-15 at
  RPE 8.\n- Walking lunges with dumbbells: 2-3 x 12 steps per leg at RPE 7
  paired with reverse Nordic curls 2 x 6-10 at RPE 7 and leg extension 2 x
  15-20 at RPE 8.\n- Core finisher: calf raises plus Copenhagen plank 2-3 
 sets each at RPE 7.\n- Activation: weighted hyperextensions: 2 x 10-15 at
  RPE 5-6 using no more than 50% of normal working load\; stop if symptoms
  rise or the next morning is worse.\n\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, k
 eep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates before and after traini
 ng.\n\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if jo
 ints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
