SUMMARY:Core + Chest/Back Strength Capacity
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3350 kcal\, 175 g protein\, 455 g carbs\, 9
 5 g fat\nMacro timing: 35-45 g protein in 4 meals\, 40-70 g carbs before 
 lifting\, and a protein-plus-carb meal after training.\nCategory: gym\nRu
 n volume: 0 km\n\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 5 min easy bike\, shoulder prep\, thoraci
 c mobility\, hip openers\, and two light press/row ramp sets.\n\n\nMain W
 ork:\n- Progression: this is the eighth strength day in the 14-day wave\;
  cap work at RPE 7-8\, use supersets\, and trim accessories before anchor
  work if recovery dips.\n- Chest volume: bench press 3 x 6-8\, incline du
 mbbell press 3 x 8-10\, dumbbell press 2 x 8-10\, pec-deck 2 x 12-15\, di
 ps 2 x 6-10\, and push-ups 2 x clean reps.\n- Back volume: lat pulldown o
 r pull-ups 3 x 8-12\, cable row or chest-supported row 3 x 8-12\, face pu
 lls 2 x 12-15\, and rear delt fly or reverse pec-deck 2 x 15-20.\n- Leg m
 aintenance: hip thrust or glute bridge 3 x 8-12\, leg extension 2 x 12-15
 \, and seated or lying hamstring curl 2 x 10-15 at RPE 7.\n- Core volume:
  Pallof press 3 x 10 per side\, side plank 2 x 30 sec per side\, plank va
 riations 2 x 30-45 sec\, hanging leg raises 2-3 sets\, weighted sit-ups 2
  x 8-12\, and kettlebell side bend or around the head kettlebell 2 x 10.\
 n\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place 
 carbohydrates before and after training.\n\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window s
 tays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
