SUMMARY:Plyometrics + Functional Power
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3600 kcal\, 170 g protein\, 550 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: 80-110 g carbs in the 2-3 hours before running\, 
 25-35 g protein after\, and another carb-heavy meal within 2 hours.\nCate
 gory: sprint\nRun volume: 3 km\n\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 10 min easy plus skips\, 
 ankling\, hip openers\, and 3 relaxed strides.\n\n\nMain Work:\n- Progres
 sion: add power volume only when jumps stay crisp and knees stay quiet th
 e next day\; sprint RPE 7-8.\n- Plyometrics: pogos 3 x 20 sec\, low broad
  jumps 4 x 2\, and med-ball slams 4 x 5 at crisp RPE 6-7 if available.\n-
  Hill sprint technique: 4-6 x 8-10 sec at sprint RPE 7-8.\n- Functional w
 ork: sled push if easy to set up or farmer carries 4 x 30 m at RPE 7.\n- 
 Core: side plank 2 x 30 sec per side or Pallof press 3 x 10 per side.\n\n
 \nRun:\n- Planned running volume: 3 km.\n\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros
 \, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates before and after tr
 aining.\n\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility i
 f joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
