SUMMARY:Plyometrics + Hill Sprint Technique
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3600 kcal\, 170 g protein\, 550 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: 80-110 g carbs in the 2-3 hours before running\, 
 25-35 g protein after\, and another carb-heavy meal within 2 hours.\nCate
 gory: sprint\nRun volume: 3 km\n\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 10-12 min easy plus leg s
 wings\, A-skips\, ankling\, and 3 relaxed strides.\n\n\nMain Work:\n- Pro
 gression: add sprint reps only when contacts stay snappy and knees stay q
 uiet the next day\; sprint RPE 7-8\, never max.\n- Plyometrics: pogos 3 x
  20 sec\, snap-downs 3 x 5\, low broad jumps 3 x 3 at crisp RPE 6-7.\n- H
 ill sprints: 4 x 10-12 sec uphill at sprint RPE 7-8\; full walk-back reco
 very.\n- Stop the sprint set if mechanics get sloppy or knees feel sharp.
 \n\n\nOptional:\n- weighted sit-ups 2 x 8-12 and side plank 2 x 30 sec pe
 r side.\n\n\nRun:\n- Planned running volume: 3 km.\n\n\nFueling:\n- Hit d
 aily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates before a
 nd after training.\n\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add
  mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
